        "instruction": "Create a proposal comparing the baseline (from D새비교) with the new product (from D새견적). \n\nBaseline:\n- Product A: Lead time 10 days\n- Product B: Lead time 20 days\n\nNew Product Data (from D새견적):\n- Product A: Price 30 million KRW\n- Product B: Price 40 million KRW\n\nConstraint: Do NOT evaluate or include price in the comparison/analysis. Only compare non-price attributes if available, or state that only price data was provided for the new product and thus no technical/commercial comparison beyond what's stated is possible. Since the prompt asks for a 'quote proposal' (견적으로 제안서), and the source only has prices, I will present the quote information clearly while noting the baseline lead times as context, but strictly adhering to 'no price evaluation' means I should not judge which is better value, just present the facts.\n\nActually, looking at the sources:\nSource 1 (D새비교): 'Product A lead time 10 days, Product B lead time 20 days'. This is the 'previously heard criteria'.\nSource 2 (D새견적): 'Product A is 30 million KRW, Product B is 40 million KRW'. This is the 'just arrived product'.\n\nThe user wants a 'proposal with quote' (견적으로 제안서). \nThe constraint is 'Do not evaluate price' (가격은 평가하지 마).\n\nSo the proposal should likely list the items, their baseline lead times (if applicable to the new product? No, the baseline IS the old criteria. The new product HAS prices. Does the new product have lead times? The source doesn't say. It only says prices.\n\nIf the new product source ONLY contains prices, and the baseline source ONLY contains lead times, there is no common attribute to compare other than listing them side-by-side.\n\nHowever, usually 'compare' implies finding differences. Here we have different attributes.\n\nLet's construct the proposal:\n1. Baseline Criteria (Previous):\n   - Product A: 10 days lead time\n   - Product B: 20 days lead time\n\n2. New Product Quote (Just Arrived):\n   - Product A: 30 million KRW\n   - Product B: 40 million KRW\n\n3. Comparison/Proposal:\n   Since no lead time is given for the new product, and no price is given for the baseline, we cannot compare lead times or prices directly against each other. We simply present the new quote alongside the known baseline standards.\n\n   Proposal Text:\n   \"Based on the previously established criteria (Product A: 10 days, Product B: 20 days lead time), here is the quote for the newly arrived products:\n   - Product A: 30 million KRW\n   - Product B: 40 million KRW\n   \n   Note: Price evaluation is excluded as requested.\""
      }
    ],
